<title>UK: Glaxo says Naramig wins UK approval.</title>
<headline>Glaxo says Naramig wins UK approval.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Glaxo Wellcome Plc said on Friday that its new anti-migraine drug Naramig had been approved for sale in Britain.</p>
<p>The company said in a research and development update that it was also developing new versions of its existing best-selling migraine drug Imigran/Imitrex. A nasal spray version was approved in the U.S. last week, the company added.</p>
<p>The company said sales of Imigran/Imitrex grew by 46 percent last year, but added that &quot;just two million out of the 26 million U.S. migraineurs have been treated with Imitrex (which) demonstrates the potential for future growth.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
